  "text": "Maqam ‘Iraq A member of the Maqam Sikah Family Maqam Index Pronunciation of ‘Iraq Click the notes and hold using the mouse to hear them play. Maqam ‘Iraq is a rare member of the Sikah maqam family , although it is more common as a modulation in the sayr of Maqam Huzam . Its scale starts with the root Jins Sikah on the tonic of B , followed by Jins Bayati on the 3 rd degree then Jins Rast on the 6 th degree. Explore other maqamat in the Maqam Sikah Family . Jayin ya Arz el-Jabal Wadih al-Safi Muwashah Jalla Man Ansha Jamalak Ensemble Ornina (Syria) Conducted by Dr. Muhammad Qadri Dalal Sama‘i ‘Iraq Tunisian Radio Orchestra Music by Yusuf Basha el-Hali Ta‘bani Ya Layla Joseph Saqr Music by Ziad Rahbani",
